## ThreadSanitizer suppressions for known false positives.
## See: https://github.com/google/sanitizers/wiki/ThreadSanitizerCppManual

## OpenSSL internal locking (CRYPTO_THREAD_* callbacks are designed for this)
race:CRYPTO_
race:SSL_
race:BIO_
race:EVP_
race:OPENSSL_

## libuv internal state
race:uv__
race:uv_

## nghttp2 internals
race:nghttp2_

## libuv threadpool barrier teardown race during server shutdown.
## csilk_server_run()/free() destroys the libuv threadpool barrier
## (pthread_barrier_destroy) while worker threads are still in
## uv_barrier_wait(). This is a server-teardown ordering issue, not a
## per-allocation race. Tracked as a known concurrency limitation.
race:uv_barrier_destroy
race:pthread_barrier_destroy

## io_uring async eventfd kernel-side race.
race:eventfd

## Epoch-based RCU in the MVCC cache (src/core/cache/mvcc_cache.c).
## Readers publish their active_epoch (release) on entry and writers only
## free a retired node once every reader's epoch has advanced past it
## (acquire). That epoch barrier makes the window race-free at runtime, but
## TSAN does not model epoch/RCU happens-before, so it flags the reader's
## plain strcmp(node->key, ...) against the writer's free(node->key)
## inside try_reclaim(). Suppressed as a known RCU false positive; the
## snapshot-integrity test (test_mvcc_cache_snapshot) still verifies
## correctness at the application level.
race:try_reclaim
race:csilk_mvcc_cache_get_view
